\]

This is one of the most important features.

Requirements:

- Accept square matrices only.
- Test invertibility.
- Use Gauss-Jordan elimination as the primary educational procedure.
- Construct the augmented matrix [A | I].
- Select valid pivots.
- Show actual elementary row operations.
- Store each intermediate matrix.
- Transform [A | I] into [I | A^-1].
- Display the inverse matrix.
- Verify the result.

Verification:

\[
AA^{-1}=I
\]

Optionally also verify:

\[
A^{-1}A=I
\]

If the input matrix is singular, display a proper Vietnamese explanation.

Never fabricate an inverse for a singular matrix.

